  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>Tech Stack & Architecture Overview</bold>\nThis document provides a high-level overview of our production technical stack, core architectural patterns, and systemic design principles. It serves as the baseline technical reference for all engineering onboarding and system development.\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Global Technology Stack Summary\n2.1 Core Runtime Environment\n2.2 Data Layer & Persistence Models\n3. Architectural Patterns & Communication Layer\n3.1 Decoupled N-Tier Topology\n3.2 Service Interaction Protocols\n4. Infrastructure, Deployment & Telemetry Pipelines\n4.1 CI/CD Orchestration Engine\n4.2 Observability & Performance Metrics\n5. Core Security & Compliance Guardrails\n5.1 In-Transit & At-Rest Protections\n5.2 Key Management Systems [1]\n<bold>2. Global Technology Stack Summary</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Core Runtime Environment [2]</bold>\nOur platform environment is split into specialized, single-responsibility technical layers to maximize scalability and isolation:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Frontend Engine:</textStyle></bold> Single-Page Application (SPA) built using React Framework, TypeScript compilation, and centralized state orchestration.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Backend Application Layer:</textStyle></bold> High-concurrency services executed via Node.js runtime and asynchronous Python micro-framework processing blocks.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Virtual Container Infrastructure:</textStyle></bold> Docker engine abstractions managed by cloud-native container clustering systems.\n<bold>2.2 Data Layer & Persistence Models</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Primary Relational Database:</textStyle></bold> PostgreSQL cluster running write-ahead logs, transaction isolation rules, and multi-region replication.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">In-Memory Session Cache:</textStyle></bold> Redis cache nodes optimized for high-speed string lookups, session serialization, and database query caching.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Object Cloud Storage:</textStyle></bold> Scalable, encrypted block object stores configured to hold structured file backups and client asset media.\n<bold>3. Architectural Patterns & Communication Layer</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Decoupled N-Tier Topology</bold>\nThe production network topology isolates user-facing client frameworks from backend logic compute nodes and persistent datastores using a layered tier approach:\n┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────┐\n│ Presenter Client│ ───&gt;  │ API Edge Gateway│ ───&gt;  │ Core App Engine │\n│  (React/TS SPA) │       │ (Reverse Proxy) │       │  (Node/FastAPI) │\n└─────────────────┘       └─────────────────┘       └───────┬─────────┘\n                                                            │\n                                                            ▼\n                                                    ┌─────────────────┐\n                                                    │ Relational Pools│\n                                                    │ (PostgreSQL Data)│\n                                                    └─────────────────┘\n<bold>3.2 Service Interaction Protocols</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Synchronous Interfacing:</textStyle></bold> RESTful endpoint logic using strict JSON payload packages passing over secure TLS 1.3 network channels.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Asynchronous Processing Pipelines:</textStyle></bold> Distributed message streaming queues handling non-blocking background tasks and system event logging.\n<bold>4. Infrastructure, Deployment & Telemetry Pipelines</bold>\n<bold>4.1 CI/CD Orchestration Engine</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Automated Continuous Integration:</textStyle></bold> Automated checking tools run static syntax analysis, security scans, and unit tests on every pull request. Code merges require a 100% pass metric.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Continuous Deployment Pipelines:</textStyle></bold> Successful trunk-branch updates automatically generate an immutable system build image and push it to production environments with zero downtime.\n<bold>4.2 Observability & Performance Metrics</bold>\nSystem telemetry metrics stream continuously into centralized monitoring clusters to maintain platform visibility:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Application APM Tracking:</textStyle></bold> Continuous P95 metric traces with automated alert triggers if API endpoint processing speeds cross 300ms.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Infrastructure Health Dumps:</textStyle></bold> Logging storage consumption, container CPU saturation flags, and database memory lock profiles every 10 seconds.\n<bold>5. Core Security & Compliance Guardrails</bold>\n<bold>5.1 In-Transit & At-Rest Protections</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Network Transport Protection:</textStyle></bold> The platform enforces global HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) and drops any connection utilizing legacy encryption layers.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Storage Cryptography Configuration:</textStyle></bold> All structural datastores and transactional archives use AES-256 block encryption strategies at the storage hardware layer.\n<bold>5.2 Key Management Systems</bold>\nSensitive credentials, token signatures, and private integration keys are never stored directly within product repositories. The container runtime injects these credentials securely from managed runtime identity stores during platform initialization.",
